<title>MOROCCO: Maghreb countries start Ramadan.</title>
<headline>Maghreb countries start Ramadan.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four Maghreb countries -- Morocco, Algeria, Tunisia and Libya -- started the Moslem holy fasting month of Ramadan on Friday.</p>
<p>The official Moroccan news agency MAP said late on Thursday that the new moon had been sighted and Ramadan would start on Friday.</p>
<p>Algeria's official news agency APS and Tunisian and Libyan television stations made similar announcements.</p>
</text>
